  "tempo": 1.12,
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "That amazing old book smell is literally the smell of the book slowly breaking",
      "start": 0.077,
      "end": 4.13
    },
    {
      "text": "down.",
      "start": 4.13,
      "end": 4.47
    },
    {
      "text": "As paper, ink, glue, and bindings age, they release volatile chemicals into the",
      "start": 4.81,
      "end": 9.425
    },
    {
      "text": "air.",
      "start": 9.425,
      "end": 9.657
    },
    {
      "text": "Different compounds can create grassy, musty, almond-like, and even vanilla-like",
      "start": 9.978,
      "end": 14.689
    },
    {
      "text": "smells.",
      "start": 14.689,
      "end": 15.118
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanillin is one of the compounds associated with that familiar sweet note.",
      "start": 15.419,
      "end": 18.814
    },
    {
      "text": "Scientists and conservators can even study these emissions to learn about the",
      "start": 19.191,
      "end": 22.989
    },
    {
      "text": "condition of aging paper.",
      "start": 22.989,
      "end": 24.274
    },
    {
      "text": "So when Bill opens a 100-year-old book and thinks it smells weirdly delicious,",
      "start": 24.642,
      "end": 28.786
    },
    {
      "text": "he is basically enjoying the smell of chemistry happening in extremely slow",
      "start": 29.063,
      "end": 32.736
    },
    {
      "text": "motion.",
      "start": 32.736,
      "end": 33.111
    }
  ],
